      "path": "src/coordinators/valuation/value-trade.ts",
      "content": "When `factsAtClose` is true but the session is outside calendar coverage, `openReadSession` supplies no `closeInstant`, so this expression silently omits the cutoff. `derive` does not filter facts by `valuationDate`; it then includes every effective execution and settlement, including those after the requested review date. Consequently, quantities and realized-to-date figures can reflect future transactions (or even return a later Closed trade) in a historical review. Handle the unavailable close explicitly rather than falling back to all-facts valuation, and add a test with an uncovered Review date and later executions.",
      "existing_code": "  const open = derive({ record: analysis, ...(options.factsAtClose \u0026\u0026 session.closeInstant \u0026\u0026 { cutoff: session.closeInstant }), valuationDate: session.tradingDate });",
